hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17376","Haddathana Yaqub, he said haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, he said haddathani Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri, and from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two leather socks."
"17377","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Musab, he said haddathana al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abi Salamah, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two leather socks and the head-cover."
"17378","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa and Husayn ibn Muhammad, they said haddathana Shayban, from Yahya, from Abi Salamah, that Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri informed him that his father informed him that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two leather socks."
"17379","Haddathana Abu Amir, haddathana Ali, meaning Ibn Mubarak, from Yahya, from Abi Salamah, he said akhbarani Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two leather socks."
"17380","Haddathana Abu Amir, haddathana Fulayh, from al-Zuhri, he said haddathani Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat a limb, then pray and not perform ablution."
"17381","Haddathana Yaqub, haddathana my father, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Haddathani Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, that his father said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cutting from a sheep shoulder, then he was called to prayer, so he threw the knife and did not perform ablution."
"17382","Haddathana Yaqub, he said haddathana my father, from Ibn Shihab, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating, cutting from a sheep shoulder, then he was called to prayer, so he prayed and did not perform ablution."
"17383","Haddathana Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri, haddathana Haywah, akhbarani Ayyash ibn Abbas, that Kulayb ibn Subayh narrated to him that al-Zibriqan narrated to him, from his uncle Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in some of his journeys, so he slept past the dawn prayer until the sun rose, they did not wake, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began with the two cycles, so he prayed them, then he established the prayer and prayed."
"17384","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, Abd Allah said, and I heard it from Abd Allah ibn Abi Shaybah at al-Kufah, he said haddathana Jafar ibn Awn, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, he said akhbarani Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him alone as a scout to Quraysh. He said: I came to the wood of Khubayb while fearing watchers, so I climbed it and loosened Khubayb, so he fell to the ground, then I withdrew not far, then I turned and did not see Khubayb, as if the earth swallowed him, and no trace of Khubayb was seen till now. Abu Abd al-Rahman said, and Ibn Abi Shaybah said to us in it from al-Zuhri, and as for my father, he narrated from him and did not mention al-Zuhri, and Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated it to us at al-Kufah, so he made it for us from al-Zuhri."
"17757","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa who said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, from so-and-so ibn Amr ibn Umayya, from his father who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat meat, or a sinew, and he did not rinse and did not touch water, then he prayed."
"17758","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayya al-Damri, from his father, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating from a shoulder, cutting from it, then he was called to prayer, so he prayed and did not perform ablution."
"17759","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amr ibn Umayya al-Damri who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two leather socks."
"17760","Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir al-Yamami narrated to us, from Abu Salama, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayya al-Damri, from his father, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two leather socks and the turban."
"17761","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Hammam, the brother of Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd al-Madani who said: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayya narrated to us, from his father who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whatever a man gives his wife, it is charity. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Hammam, the brother of Abd al-Razzaq."
"17762","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Jafar ibn Umayya al-Damri, from his father, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut from a shoulder and eat, then the caller to prayer came to him, so he threw the knife, then stood for prayer and did not perform ablution."
"17763","Yunus narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, who said: Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayya, that his father told him that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two leather socks."
